== Match report ==

=== Jarin 1–0 Nusaraya ===
[[Jarin national football team|Jarin]] needed just one goal to see off [[Nusaraya national football team|Nusaraya]] in [[Castramara]], with Petros Shimora scoring the match's only goal in the 25th minute. Nusaraya pressed late, but Jarin's structure held and the Mesogean side opened their campaign with a narrow victory.

Goalscorer: Petros Shimora (25')

=== Asikyira 4–4 United Midlands ===
[[United Midlands national football team|United Midlands]] and [[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]] shared the highest-scoring match of the day in [[Sanropura]]. Oliver Hartley opened the scoring, United Midlands twice moved back in front through Samuel Wren and Ethan Mercer, and Asikyira answered through Amadou Baal, Boubacar Sarr, Idrissa Koné and Ousmane Gueye before Thomas Vale's late equaliser rescued a point for the Lurandians.

Goalscorers: Oliver Hartley (5'), Amadou Baal (9'), Samuel Wren (17'), Ethan Mercer (36'), Boubacar Sarr (40'), Idrissa Koné (44'), Ousmane Gueye (70'), Thomas Vale (87')

=== Burawa 4–2 Daras ===
[[Burawa national football team|Burawa]] and [[Daras national football team|Daras]] produced the wildest finish of the day in [[San Chorche]]. Burawa went two up through Petre Xirsi and Qaasim Dhaxol, only for Daras to level the match late through Chen Zihang and Wang Yuchen. The game then swung back in Burawa's favour in stoppage time, as Yaxye Cumar and Xirsi Shire struck in quick succession to secure the points.

Goalscorers: Petre Xirsi (22'), Qaasim Dhaxol (85'), Chen Zihang (87'), Wang Yuchen (90'), Yaxye Cumar (90+1'), Xirsi Shire (90+2')

=== Varkana 2–0 Pangkajene ===
[[Varkana national football team|Varkana]] made a fast start in [[Telukuba]], with Hugo Loria scoring inside the opening minute to settle the match early. [[Pangkajene national football team|Pangkajene]] stayed in the contest for long spells, but Luka Paliashvili's late strike made sure of the result and gave Varkana a comfortable-looking win on the scoreline.

Goalscorers: Hugo Loria (1'), Luka Paliashvili (84')

=== Orma 0–0 Sarta ===
[[Orma national football team|Orma]] and [[Sarta national football team|Sarta]] played out a cagey goalless draw in [[Pangkalsimpang]]. Both sides were organised and disciplined, but neither could find the decisive moment needed to break the deadlock.

=== Aetolia 1–1 Louyang ===
[[Louyang national football team|Louyang]] took an early lead in [[Valparaíso]] through Chen Minghao, but [[Aetolia national football team|Aetolia]] responded before the half-hour mark when Nikos Stavridis equalised. The rest of the match remained tight, with both sides settling for a point after a balanced encounter.

Goalscorers: Chen Minghao (7'), Nikos Stavridis (34')

== Summary ==

The second matchday featured 19 goals, a dramatic draw, one narrow win, one late two-goal win, two draws, and two high-tempo thrillers. United Midlands and Asikyira shared the day's highest-scoring match, while Burawa's late escape against Daras provided the most dramatic finish.

